# The repo is developed on Windows but builds on macOS and Linux, so the files
# the Unix build depends on must arrive with LF endings. A CRLF build.sh fails
# with "bad interpreter" because the \r ends up part of the shebang path, and a
# CRLF Makefile is worse than it looks: the \r lands inside variable values, so
# NAME := powder silently becomes "powder\r" and the binary is written to a
# filename nothing else refers to.
* text=auto

*.sh      text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
